== fuller page ==
C4's grammar has no error state. Its fallback type is word: anything that
does not resolve "stands for itself" [word]. Every token either resolves or
keeps its own text, so a line can always be rebuilt, byte for byte, from its
pieces.

The same rule comes back at every height [heights]. A run nobody registered
stays a word. A line nobody could parse stays, verbatim, as a comment. A
check nobody could run is reported, never claimed as passed. The language
"always has somewhere honest to put what it could not read" [honest].

"Could not check" is a third answer, beside yes and no, and it "must never
share a channel with 'checked and passed'" [third]. The tools mean it:
tv1cr answers a question it cannot answer with its own exit code, 2, and
says so [exit2]. When it overwrites a cell, it keeps the old value
[trampled].

Rulings work the same way. In the shop's question bank, Q607 was DEFAULTED
on 2026-10-19 and RULED on 2026-10-20; the ruling is a new row, and the
default stays above it [ruled]. To log, in C4, "is to ADD an atom, never to
edit the past" [log].

C4-LANG is careful here too. Keeping everything is right where dropping a
human sentence would be the harm, and wrong where an unreadable input means
the world is not as assumed. It is "a choice about which failure you
prefer, not a strict improvement" [local].

