== narration ==
# Take A, "the company talks to you": every voice speaks to the listener.
[picture A]
narrator: Here are Pin's shelves. Look how full they are.
pin: I keep every word. Even the new ones.
spoke: I found one nobody knows. Zib. Is that a word?
pin: A new word is a word, too. Up it goes.
narrator: And this box with the question mark? That's for things we could not check.
pin: They have a box of their own. I keep it all, for you.
[fuller A]
narrator [word]: {C4|C four}'s grammar has no error state. Anything that doesn't match stands for itself, as a word.
spoke [heights]: The same rule comes back at every height. A word nobody registered stays a word. A line nobody could read stays, as a comment. A check nobody could run gets reported, never passed.
pin [honest]: There's always somewhere honest to put what we couldn't read. I like that.
narrator [third]: Could not check is a third answer, next to yes and no. It must never sound like checked and passed.
spoke [exit2]: One of the shop's tools even has its own number for it. It says, out loud, I can't answer that.
pin [trampled]: And when it writes over something, it keeps the old one. Just like me.
narrator [ruled]: Rulings too. When a question gets its ruling, the ruling is a new row, and the old guess stays right there above it.
pin [log]: To log is to add, never to edit the past.
narrator [local]: And the language book is honest about this too. Keeping everything is a choice about which mistake you'd rather make. Sometimes stopping is the right thing to do.

# Take B, "the lap reader": one close voice reads to you; Spoke and Pin
# mostly talk to each other, and turn to you only in a short aside.
[picture B]
narrator: Pin keeps every word. A new word is a word, too.
spoke: Pin. Zib. I found a zib.
pin: Then zib goes on the shelf.
narrator: What we could not check has a box of its own.
spoke: The question box is getting full.
pin: Good. Pin keeps it all.
[fuller B]
narrator [word]: {C4|C four}'s grammar has no error state. Its fallback type is word: anything that does not resolve stands for itself.
narrator [heights]: The same rule comes back at every height. A word stays a word. An unreadable line stays, verbatim, as a comment. A check that could not be run is reported, never asserted.
narrator [honest]: The language always has somewhere honest to put what it could not read.
pin [third]: Could not check is its own answer. It never shares a channel with checked and passed.
spoke [exit2]: The table tool says it with its own exit code, Pin. Two.
pin [trampled]: And it keeps the old value when it writes a new one.
narrator [ruled]: In the question bank, {Q607|Q six oh seven} was defaulted one day and ruled the next. Both rows are still there.
pin [log]: To log is to add an atom, never to edit the past.
narrator [local]: Totality is a choice about which failure you prefer, not a strict improvement. The language book says so itself.

